local a={"Win a hand after declaring Riichi. To declare Riichi, your hand must be Menzenchin (closed) and in Tenpai (one tile away from winning).","Win a hand without any Terminal tiles (1/9 Man, 1/9 Pin, 1/9 Sou) or Honor tiles (Winds and Dragons).","Win a closed hand by Tsumo (drawing the winning tile yourself).","Win a hand with a triplet or quad of your Seat Wind.","Win a hand with a triplet or quad of the current Round Wind.","Win a hand with a triplet or quad of Dragon tiles (White, Green, or Red).","Win a closed hand with four sequences and a pair that is not Dragon, Seat Wind, or Round Wind tiles. The winning tile must complete a sequence on a two-sided wait (e.g., 6-7 waiting for 5 or 8).","Win a closed hand with two identical sequences (the same numbers in the same suit).","Win a hand by Ron on the tile another player attempts to add to an open triplet to make a Kan. (With Thirteen Orphans, you can also call Ron on a closed Kan.)","Win a hand on the tile drawn from the Dead Wall immediately after calling a Kan.","Win a hand by Tsumo on the last tile drawn from the Tile Wall.","Win a hand by Ron on the final discard after the last tile is drawn from the Tile Wall.","Win a hand within one turn after declaring Riichi, with no intervening calls (Chii, Pon, or Kan) by any player.","The next tile in sequence after the revealed Dora indicator.","Red 5 Man, Red 5 Pin, Red 5 Sou. (Also known as Red Dora.)","In 3-player mahjong, declare Kita to set aside a North Wind tile and count it as bonus Dora. (North Wind tiles kept in your hand do not count as bonus Dora.)","(Swallow Return) Win a hand by Ron on another player\'s Riichi declaration discard.","Win a hand by Ron on the first tile another player discards after they declare a Kan.","Win a hand with four open sets (formed by Chii, Pon, or Kan) and a single-tile wait to complete the pair.","Declare Riichi on your first discard, before any player makes a tile call (Chii, Pon, or Kan).","Win a hand with three triplets or quads of the same number, one in each suit (Man, Pin, and Sou).","Win a hand with three quads (Kans).","Win a hand with four triplets or quads.","Win a hand with three concealed triplets or quads.","Win a hand with two triplets or quads of different Dragons (White, Green, or Red) and a pair of the third.","Win a hand containing only Terminal tiles (1/9 Man, 1/9 Pin, 1/9 Sou) and Honor tiles (Winds and Dragons).","Win a hand with seven distinct pairs.","Win a hand with at least one Terminal or Honor tile in every set and in the pair.","Win a hand with the sequences 123, 456, and 789 in the same suit.","Win a hand with three sequences of the same numbers, one in each suit (Man, Pin, and Sou).","Win a hand containing tiles from all five categories: Man, Pin, Sou, Winds, and Dragons.","Win a hand with three triplets or quads of consecutive numbers in the same suit.","Win a closed hand with two pairs of identical sequences (the same numbers in the same suit within each pair).","Win a hand with at least one Terminal tile (1/9 Man, 1/9 Pin, 1/9 Sou) in every set and in the pair.","Win a hand with tiles from only one suit (Man, Pin, or Sou) and Honor tiles (Winds and Dragons).","(Pure Triple Sequence) Win a hand with three identical sequences (the same numbers in the same suit).","Win a hand with tiles from only one suit (Man, Pin, or Sou).","At an exhaustive draw, score a Mangan if all your discards are Terminal or Honor tiles and none have been called by other players.","Win a hand by Tsumo on the last tile drawn from the Tile Wall, which must be 1 Pin. (5 Han)","Win a hand by Ron on the final discard after the last tile is drawn from the Tile Wall. That discard must be 9 Pin. (5 Han)","Win a hand as the dealer with your initial 14 tiles.","Win a hand by Tsumo as a non-dealer on your first draw, before any player makes a tile call (Chii, Pon, or Kan).","Win a hand with a triplet or quad of each Dragon (White, Green, and Red).","Win a hand with four concealed triplets or quads.","Win a hand with only Honor tiles (Winds and Dragons).","Win a hand with only green-colored tiles: 2/3/4/6/8 Sou and/or Green Dragons.","Win a hand with only Terminal tiles (1/9 Man, 1/9 Pin, 1/9 Sou).","Win a hand with one of each of the 13 Terminal and Honor tiles, plus a duplicate of any one of them.","Win a hand with triplets or quads of three different Winds, plus a pair of the fourth Wind.","Win a hand with four quads (Kans).","Win a closed hand with 1112345678999 in a single suit (Man, Pin, or Sou), plus one additional tile of the same suit.","Win a hand by Ron as a non-dealer before your first draw and before any player makes a tile call (Chii, Pon, or Kan).","Win a hand with seven pairs, one pair of each Pin tile from 2 through 8.","Win a hand with seven pairs, one pair of each Sou tile from 2 through 8.","Win a hand with seven pairs, one pair of each Man tile from 2 through 8.","(Three Years on a Stone) Win a hand with Double Riichi and either Under the Sea or Under the River.","Win a hand with four concealed triplets or quads after waiting on a single tile type to complete the pair.","Win a hand by drawing a duplicate while already holding one of each of the 13 Terminal and Honor tiles. Any of these tiles can be the winning tile.","Win a hand while already holding 1112345678999 in a single suit, with any tile of that suit as the winning tile.","Win a hand with a triplet or quad of each Wind (East, South, West, and North).","Win a hand with seven pairs, one pair of each Honor tile (Winds and Dragons).","The hand ends in an abortive draw if all four players discard the same Wind tile on their first turn and no tile calls have been made.","The hand ends in an abortive draw when two or more players have called a total of four Kans.","You may declare an abortive draw before your first discard if you hold at least 9 different Terminal and Honor tiles and no player has made a tile call.","The hand ends in an abortive draw when all four players have declared Riichi.","A basic winning hand in Bloodshed Skirmish with no yaku other than bonus yaku, if any.","Win a hand on the tile drawn from the Dead Wall immediately after calling a Kan.","Win a hand by Ron on the first tile another player discards after they declare a Kan.","Win a hand by Ron on the tile another player attempts to add to an open triplet to make a Kan.","Win a hand by Tsumo on the last tile drawn from the Tile Wall, or by Ron on the discard that follows.","Have four identical tiles in total across your hand and called sets (including Kans).","Win a hand with tiles from only one suit (Man, Pin, or Sou).","Win a hand with seven pairs. Four identical tiles may count as two pairs.","Win a hand with at least one Terminal tile (1/9 Man, 1/9 Pin, 1/9 Sou) in every set and in the pair.","Win a hand with four open triplets or quads (formed by Pon or Kan).","Win a hand with four triplets or quads and a pair, all in the same suit. (Full Flush + All Triplets)","Win a hand with All Triplets using only tiles numbered 2, 5, or 8.","Win a hand with seven pairs, including four identical tiles counted as two pairs.","Win a hand with seven pairs, all in the same suit. (Full Flush + Seven Pairs)","Win a hand with tiles from only one suit and at least one Terminal tile in every set and in the pair. (Full Flush + Terminals in All Sets)","Win a hand with four open triplets or quads and a pair, all in the same suit. (Full Flush + Single Wait after 4 Triplets)","Win a hand as the dealer with your initial 14 tiles.","Win a hand by Tsumo as a non-dealer on your first draw, before any player makes a tile call (Chii, Pon, or Kan).","Win a hand with seven pairs in a single suit, including four identical tiles counted as two pairs. (Full Flush + Seven Pairs with One Duplicate)","Win a hand with four quads (Kans).","Win a hand with four quads and a pair, all in the same suit. (Full Flush + Four Quads)"}return a